A||||23||Pheagey||Scariest driving situation.||||9||
Z||000000||Pheagey||10-24-2001||12:19 AM||||Mine was just this evening. Just after a typical Florida rain spell i was turning at an intersection (as the light turned red):<BR>intersection turn at 25MPH, no so bad; <BR>hydroplaneing, no so bad; not seeing the lane dividers 'cause there's no paint on the road; not so bad.<BR>Altogether: VERY bad!<BR>Needless to say I made it (and kissed my car as soonas I got home).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Pheagey Grean<BR>"The time to talk is over. The time for diplomacy is over, the time for bluffing is over. The time to kick some f!@king as$ is now."<P>'88 coupe 'Hotwheels'<P>Http://www.LithiumEffects.com/car.html<P>Kills: '97 Civic Auto,<BR>Killed by: -||||reg||9
Z||000001||Cozmo||10-24-2001||02:10 AM||||What is also scary is the paint they use for lane dividers is SLIPPERY!<BR>Glad to hear you didn't "ditch it" or anything...<BR><P>------------------<BR><B>BobC</B><BR><B>'85 2M6 Targa</B><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/targsig.jpg"> <BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||BN Boomer||10-24-2001||04:55 AM||||Try driving a Fiero on snow or ice. Man knows no greater pucker factor.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||10-24-2001||05:19 AM||||Driving a Fiero in ice and snow is easy.  Try sliding sideways down Black Mtn in an 18 wheeler.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BN Boomer||10-24-2001||06:07 AM||||I'd rather drive an 18 wheeler in snow or ice than a Fiero. Fieros have too little contact pressure and short wheel base vehicles really suck in slippery stuff. Combine the two and you have a recipe for spinning out.<P>Of course, I'd probably never drive an 18 wheeler again, either. Real men use locomotives.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Greg, aka Boomer<BR>Red 85 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.gmemd.com/locomotives/naf/images/sd70sm.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jake_Dragon||10-24-2001||07:36 AM||||I was driving back to work from lunch when it started to rain. When I got behind a civic, the driver was talking on a cell phone and not staying in his lane. I decided to get away from him and attempted to pass. He nearly hit me twice before I got around him, then he was mad because I passed him and started to pass me! About that time traffic started to stop and when I put on the breaks nothing happened, pumping didn't help and I was headed for a School bus. Letting off the breaks so I could steer I took the car off the road and tagged a small tree. Some damage but nothing that cant be fixed. The thing that ticked me off the most is not one of the other drivers stopped to see if I was ok.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"><B>1985 GT</B></FONT><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt.GIF"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pheagey||10-24-2001||08:39 AM||||Jake_Dragon,<BR>   That's Florida for you.when I was up in WV it was nothing ot have a school bus to stop and the driver to help...(Don't get wrong I wouldn't wanna drive in WV wiht my 4bange or with there winters).<BR>   Anyways...<P>------------------<BR>Pheagey Grean<BR>"The time to talk is over. The time for diplomacy is over, the time for bluffing is over. The time to kick some f!@king as$ is now."<P>'88 coupe 'Hotwheels'<P>Http://www.LithiumEffects.com/car.html<P>Kills: '97 Civic Auto,<BR>Killed by: -||||reg||1
Z||000007||K2m4||10-24-2001||12:06 PM||||Heres one for you...i live on a reletively busy road between 2 towns, speed limit 45 miles an hour ...coming home the other night late from work at about 10 pm i slow down put my blinker on to turn left into my driveway.  halfway into my driveway i get plugged in the ass end ( driver side rear tire more like) from a guy following me at a very high rate of speed. i am trying to make a left hand turn and dick head cruising at about 60 tries to pass me ON THE LEFT HAND SIDE..yes the side im making a turn to. He hits me so hard the engine was ripped from the car. I get out and look at my trashed fiero at the base of my driveway mind you and hes all drunk as a skunk with a bashed in face from his windshield and air bag. he got a DWI. i didnt get hurt other than banged up pretty good. If he had hit me 2 secs earlier i wouldnt be here writing this. <BR>May my 86 2M4 with 168,000 miles strong as a horse duke rest in peace. This is a true story. All my naighbors know how much of a fiero fanactic and when they canme out they were in awwww that one of kerms cars was dead. That car was beautifull. ok im going to cry now!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Kerm<BR>86 2m4 (dead)<BR>86 GT<BR>88 2m4 (my new daily driver)<BR> ||||reg||9
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||10-24-2001||12:45 PM||||Ok... driving the GreenGT with the new 3.1 recently installed.  Get on the highway headed for work and already there is an 18 wheeler going slow in the lane in front of me- so I kick it down, move to the left lane for a normal pass.  As I'm about 1/2 way down the length of the 18 Wheeler, he puts on his turn signal to pull into the left lane (my lane)!  So I flip on my headlights and lay on the horn (like he can hear that- ha).  I start to move a little onto the shoulder when I notice the guard railing approaching quickly (70-75mph).  So I start to slow down and hit the brakes just as my driver's side wheels go off the shoulder and my right wheels are on the rumble strip. Somehow (too quick to know for sure) The car flips around backwards... I'm now traveling 70mph backwards (with the auto tranny in drive) staring at the back wheels of an 18 wheeler.  I also see the still-approaching guard rail in rearview mirror.  I know that if I hit that rail, I'll be twisted sideways under the rear sets of dualies on the semi!  Luckily my car skids to a stop within 6 inches of the rail.  I sit for a moment (staring into oncoming traffic from the edge of the road) and pull a little farther off the edge of the road and grip the wheel tightly...and breath.  I proceeded to call work and inform them that I'd be running late.  <P>-Within 2 weeks, the tranny was shot on my car and it was back in the shop for a 4spd OD!  Really the only good thing about the incident.<P>Second place to that would have to be rolling my Suzuki Samuari when I was 17... but that's a whole 'nother story.  Maybe another time (I've got pics of that <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||recluse||10-24-2001||05:08 PM||||this was mine<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newspaper2.jpg"> ||||reg||11
Z||000010||Voytek||10-24-2001||05:17 PM||||OUCH!!!<P>I love my Fieros in the winter, BTW.  Put a bit extra weight in the front and you can outhandle many cars on the road.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||MinnGreenGT||10-24-2001||05:56 PM||||Recluse... what the heck happened!?!||||reg||4
Z||000012||rogergarrison||10-24-2001||06:52 PM||||Out on one of my ritual weekend cruises in the Hocking Hills / Wayne Nat. Forest running all the great hilly, twisy, nicely maintained, practicly deserted back roads. I was running 60's mph thru all those signs marked with zigzags at 25 and 30 mph and doing fine, went around one that someone else ran off of and sprayed dirt n gravel all over the turn, I went around it like a sprint car.....really scary stuff. Lucky no one coming other way as i was practicly sideways the rest of the way around.<P>My friend with the Porsche S went on her first cruise with the Ohio Porsche club. It was pouring rain thru the SE hills, She was keeping up with a 911 T and he made a turn following the rest and she turned her wheels but hydroplaned clear off the road into someones front yard. No damage just a little mud.||||reg||1
Z||000013||recluse||10-24-2001||11:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>Recluse... what the heck happened!?!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I let my anger get the best of me, or should I say my Fiero.  I was on my lunch break at work and was mad and aggrivated with my job. On my way to the store and was just driving too fast around this curve, 65 in a 35 zone and took the curve halfway in the other lane and a car was coming and when I jurked it back into my lane the backend went out and thats where I ended up. It was not a good day.  Now I have a $4,000 parts car!||||reg||1
Z||000014||sqoach||10-25-2001||12:07 AM||||Well, my scariest driving situation was in our bronco. I was visiting my girlfriend at the time. She took her car, and I followed her in the bronc. Dirt roads the whole way into town. I was going about 35 mph and hit a BIG patch of sand. I guess the city decided to fill in this big hole with sand. Dumb@sses! Anyway, as I hit the sand, I start to slide to the right heading for a ditch. I try to turn, but nothing happens. WHAM! I hit a big sewage pipe and ramp over it! I'm flying outta my seat. I see my cd's fly in the air, onto the dash. CRASH!...into the ditch. I'm clutching the steering wheel and just stare ahead.<BR>I ended up with a flat tire and a dented steel rim! My dad was none too happy.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">              <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000015||fierobaby||10-25-2001||08:38 AM||||mine was one night just about a week ago my friend took me out in her truck to learn to drive.. it was raining I figured oh I'll be ok! NOT! I took a turn and the back end went the other way I was like HOLY @$%# I almost hit a telephone pole...but hey keep this down... no one knows I was driving with her||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cheever3000||10-25-2001||07:59 PM||||Does offroad count?  I was riding shotgun with my sandbuggy partner in Little Sahara State Park out in western Oklahoma.  We were going full speed up a long slope, not real steep but big enough it's fairly high at the top.  We had been there the night before.  Either it was not the same dune, or the wind had cut off the back side overnight, because when we crested the top we found ourselves in the air floating <B>over</B> some guys on ATC's playing on the other side.  They looked up at us, we looked down on them through the expanded-metal floor of the buggy.  I looked at my friend with the "been nice knowin' ya" expression, then we hit the flat sand at the bottom and the engine died.  Still alive & no broken bones, we got a ride back to return with the 4x4 & tools. Found out we merely broke the distributor bug.  ||||reg||1
Z||000017||malacite||10-25-2001||08:50 PM||||my scariest driving moment...<BR>well let me say that this accident kept me sober.<P>i was driving a nissan pickup nown a curvy, hilly, connecticut road in the winter. doint somthing like 95mph. my friend was in the passenger seat, and the two 15's were thumping away in the back providing distraction. anyway i looked down at the radio, to turn it up, and when i looked back at the road i saw a tree.<P>faaark!<BR>i cut the wheel turned, the truck sideways and rolled it four times. both my friend and i were thrown from the truck, i was unconsius for like ten minutes. my friend reported the truck stolen and limped home.<P>the moral of the story...don't drink and drive. i'm not farking around here! i am lucky to alive.<P>------------------<BR>Malacite<P>Grendel-88 Fiero,tech 4<BR>'94 Saturn SW2 DOHC||||reg||9
Z||000018||CoolBlue87GT||10-25-2001||10:18 PM||||Some of these stories are horrid, glad they ended without losing any members. Losing the cars were a shame.<P>My scariest drive was comming back from the Williamsburg show. <P>Ten hours into the trip I hit a down pour that lasted from Georgia thru mid Florida. At one point the Cherokee I was towing my Fiero with, started hydroplaning at 75 mph. The trailer started comming around. No steering or braking at all.<P>All I could see was broken blue plastic pieces all over the highway - my life started passing before my eyes, then, slowly, I was able to regain control - I saved it !<P>But oh lord, it scared the hell out of me. I found the next exit and pulled off and thanked god for helping me. <P>Took 30 min to get enough nerve to get back on the road.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Delttow_1.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 10-26-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000019||BN Boomer||10-26-2001||05:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CoolBlue87GT:<P><B>No steering or braking at all.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Fuuny how that always happens when your front wheels are off the ground, ain't it?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Brian87egotrip||10-26-2001||08:45 AM||||my scariest moment?  ANY TIME I RIDE WITH MY WIFE!!<P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000021||crash||10-26-2001||08:58 AM||||AMEN!!!!! Brian  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000022||btoth||10-26-2001||09:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by K2m4:<BR><B>Heres one for you...i live on a reletively busy road between 2 towns, speed limit 45 miles an hour ...coming home the other night late from work at about 10 pm i slow down put my blinker on to turn left into my driveway.  halfway into my driveway i get plugged in the ass end ( driver side rear tire more like) from a guy following me at a very high rate of speed. i am trying to make a left hand turn and dick head cruising at about 60 tries to pass me ON THE LEFT HAND SIDE..yes the side im making a turn to. He hits me so hard the engine was ripped from the car. I get out and look at my trashed fiero at the base of my driveway mind you and hes all drunk as a skunk with a bashed in face from his windshield and air bag. he got a DWI. i didnt get hurt other than banged up pretty good. If he had hit me 2 secs earlier i wouldnt be here writing this. <BR>May my 86 2M4 with 168,000 miles strong as a horse duke rest in peace. This is a true story. All my naighbors know how much of a fiero fanactic and when they canme out they were in awwww that one of kerms cars was dead. That car was beautifull. ok im going to cry now!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Kerm<BR>86 2m4 (dead)<BR>86 GT<BR>88 2m4 (my new daily driver)<BR> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's how I lost my first Fiero.<P>I was just three weeks after I rear-ended a Geo Tracker in the rain.  (Technically my fault, but the lady even said she slammed on her brakes because someone pulled out in front of her... her's were just better than mine.)  The only damage to my car was my missing emblem and the absorber under the bumber.  The body shop painted my entire front end.  Just in time for Senior Prom! Good deal!<P>Well my friend and I were out for a drive on a state road (45 mph zone) one night and decided to head for home.  The road ended at another street which was out of the way so I pulled into a driveway.  Looked both ways, so did my friend.  The problem:  one of those big little tykes mailboxes in the way and lines of trees around the twisty road.  But we still didn't see anything.<P>Pulled out, had to make a left turn to get back onto the road I wanted to be on.  Couldn't turn the blinker on because the wheel was still turned the wrong way after pulling out quickly and it took me a minute to turn the wheel at a dead stop to make the turn.  As soon as I start to turn I hear this really loud horn... the kind that just scares you if you aren't expecting it... and then SMASH! my car gets bumped back straight the way I was facing before the turn and I see the car keep going off into the ditch on the left-hand side of the road.  We didn't feel anything, no one was hurt luckily.<P>The guy ran out of his car to see if we were OK, I said we were.  I got out and realized that my whole front end was smashed to the right side of the car... inches from where my legs where.  Headlights still popped up, radio still on, but the car had stalled for some reason.  The car was in the middle of the three way intersection so we had to move it, for some reason we decided to push it instead of drive it.  I wonder now if I even tried to turn the car back on... I must have confused.<P>The guy was an officer in training and he didn't even know what number to call for the police.  Of course, I didn't know what county I was in.  Hours later, Sherrif arrived, took our statements.  (This was after the parents arrived.)  Insurance companies battled it out because he showed no signs of braking... even after he hit me he never thought the hit the brakes, and he never signaled that he was passing, etc.  But I never put my signal on either...  eventually found me not at fault anyway but my car was totalled.  Got $2000 for a car I payed $700 for.  But it was still sad.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000023||CoolBlue87GT||10-26-2001||11:00 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B> Funny how that always happens when your front wheels are off the ground, ain't it?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yea, that was to much weight for it.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Delttow1.jpg">  <BR>That stupid U-haul trailer was 2100 lbs empty. That's why I'm looking real hard at the aluminum trailer that's 830 lbs.<P>That would put the front wheels back on the ground!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 10-26-2001).]||||reg||1
